# Chase Content Graphics

**Visual SSOT:** the live product CSS/components, exposed as **social export frames** in
[`dashboard/content_export/`](../../dashboard/content_export/README.md).

**Rulebook + transitional PIL fallback:** [`Alphakiller1/chase-content-engine`](https://github.com/Alphakiller1/chase-content-engine)

**Bridge doc in this repo:** [`docs/CHASE_CONTENT_PLAN.md`](../../docs/CHASE_CONTENT_PLAN.md)

## Authority

| Concern | Where |
|---------|--------|
| **Visual chrome for daily graphics** | `dashboard/content_export/*_frame.html` reusing `mlbma_design_system.css`, `theme.css`, `landing_dashboard.css`, `mlbma_assets.js` |
| Report *rules* (canvas, header, no win-prob, opinions, fail-closed) | `chase-content-engine/design/CONTENT_DESIGN_CONTRACT.md` |
| Daily schedule, report contracts, opinion overlays, PIL fallback renderer | `chase-content-engine` (`render.py` = transitional) |
| AI concept mockups only | `chase-content-engine/design/CHATGPT_IMAGE_MOCKUP_PROMPT.md` |
| Slate / offense / trajectory CSVs | this repo (`mlbma-pipeline/data`) |
| Dashboard UI tokens | `design/MLBMA_CURSOR_DESIGN_CONTRACT.md` (this repo) |

## Rules

1. Do **not** invent a parallel template catalog (T1–T5, etc.) or a second brand system. Reuse
   the existing tokens/classes — the export frames must consume design-system tokens, never
   redefine `--bg` / `--ca-brand` / metric colors.
2. **Preferred finals = screenshot the website export frames** (`migrate → validate → open
   frame with `?bundle=` → Playwright 1080×1350 @2x → human approve). The content-engine
   `render.py` PIL output is a transitional/offline fallback, not the polish target.
3. Image models may produce **concept mockups** with logo placeholders only — never drawn
   Chase/MLB marks, never publish those as posts.
4. Do not weaken the content-engine design contract; the frames *fulfill* it (compact header,
   metallic headings, dimensional cards, **no win-prob on Morning Slate**, run-separation
   ranking, league-anchored metric colors, real logos, fail-closed data).
5. `outputs/push_instagram.py` may publish captions/URLs; it must not invent layout. Image URLs
   should point at approved frame screenshots (or the fallback engine PNGs).
6. Opinions are human editorial overlays (`MY BET` / `LEAN` / `WATCH` / `PASS` / `NO OPINION`) —
   never auto-inherited from model projections.
7. `dashboard/content_export/` frames are **new files** — do not reorder or re-nest the live
   dashboard product sections to build them (structure lock).

## When asked to “make a graphic” here

Point at the export frames first (open with `?bundle=`, screenshot at 1080×1350 @2x), keep the
content-engine contract as the rulebook, and only change data-contract code (CSV fields /
freshness) if the upstream data itself needs work.
